  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of BASH REDIRECTION: THE FIELD MANUAL. `2>&1 > file` and `> file 2>&1` look like the same command typed in a different mood — one files both streams, the other leaves stderr on your terminal. This 10-page field manual walks the fd table from `dup2` up through heredocs, process substitution and `pipefail`, so you can read any redirection left to right and know exactly where every byte goes. Save it for the next time a cron job swears it succeeded.",
